Number = {1},
Pages = {63-81},
Month = {JAN-MAR},
Abstract = {This article studies the linkage made in media discourse between the
   September 11 terror attacks and globalization. Analysis of the prestige,
   national, and regional American press reveals three principal frames
   that support issue cultures that enhance state power and promote
   neo-liberal economic policy. These frames also provide an inadvertent
   cover for unilateral United States foreign policy interests and thus
   lend support to those theorists who argue that globalization is a
   distraction that hinders a productive analysis of international
   politics.},
