Abstract = {This study revisits the question of whether committees are biased in
   their policy outputs-pursuing policies at odds with noncommittee
   members. We find evidence that committees in the House are biased: Most
   committees are either more divided than the larger membership in the
   House, or there is a greater consensus within the committee than among
   noncommittee members. These patterns extend across all types of
   committees.},
